  ('709974936964785419', 'Los Reyes', 2005, 'Family, Soap', 'Marcelo Tinelli', null, 'Cony Camelo, Enrique Carriazo, Jery Sandoval, Margarita Muñoz, Géraldine Zivic, Diego Trujillo, Jacqueline Arenal, Nataly Umaña', null, 'Los Reyes is a telenovela filmed in Colombia and produced by the Colombian network, RCN. It debuted in 2005 and is available via RCN cable TV in the United States.', 'Los Reyes is a telenovela filmed in Colombia and produced by the Colombian network, RCN. It debuted in 2005 and is available via RCN cable TV in the United States.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/gVadEZSakesdGRJzq7HbQh7yKyS.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:19505'),
  ('676140692602203718', 'Los ricos también lloran', 1979, 'Drama, Soap', 'Inés Rodena', null, 'Verónica Castro, Rogelio Guerra, Rocío Banquells, Augusto Benedico, Alicia Rodriguez, Rafael Banquells, Marilú Elízaga, Yolanda Merida', 'NR', 'Popular telenovela produced in Mexico in 1979, starring Verónica Castro, Rogelio Guerra and Rocío Banquells. Castro also sang the theme Aprendí a Llorar, a song written by Lolita de la Colina. The telenovela was produced by Chilean Valentín Pimstein and Carlos Romero, it was directed by Rafael Banquells. The story was written by Inés Rodena and adapted by Valeria Philips.', 'Popular telenovela produced in Mexico in 1979, starring Verónica Castro, Rogelio Guerra and Rocío Banquells. Castro also sang the theme Aprendí a Llorar, a song written by Lolita de la Colina. The telenovela was produced by Chilean Valentín Pimstein and Carlos Romero, it was directed by Rafael Banquells. The story was written by Inés Rodena and adapted by Valeria Philips.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/bYrC9ReL44aNI6uxAYSGN50r7Yb.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:12680'),
  ('546944654074048594', 'Los ricos también lloran', 2022, 'Soap', 'Carlos Bardasano', null, 'Sebastián Rulli, Claudia Martín, Fabiola Guajardo, Guillermo García Cantú, Azela Robinson, Henry Zakka, Mimi Morales, Arturo Barba', 'TV-14', 'Mariana is a poor young woman who is left alone in the world and must make her way in life. When she saves the life of Alberto Salvatierra, in gratitude he takes her to his house where she meets Luis Alberto Salvatierra and they fall deeply in love. To carry on their relationship, Mariana will have to overcome obstacles of social class, education and traumas, while being surrounded by ambitions and betrayals. When Mariana and Luis Alberto are able to realize their love, life will bring them a tragedy: the loss of their son.', 'Mariana is a poor young woman who is left alone in the world and must make her way in life. When she saves the life of Alberto Salvatierra, in gratitude he takes her to his house where she meets Luis Alberto Salvatierra and they fall deeply in love. To carry on their relationship, Mariana will have to overcome obstacles of social class, education and traumas, while being surrounded by ambitions and betrayals. When Mariana and Luis Alberto are able to realize their love, life will bring them a tragedy: the loss of their son.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/egFsGUUrNuxvh0h6i6hylfYwVao.jpg', 1, 'tmdb:tv:157925'),
  ('330754210933528988', 'Los Serrano', 2003, 'Comedy, Family, Drama', 'Daniel Écija, Álex Pina', 'Germán Aparicio, David Lorenzo, Verónica Marzá', 'Antonio Resines, Jesús Bonilla, Antonio Molero, Alejo Sauras, Natalia Sánchez, Víctor Elías, Goizalde Núñez, Alexandra Jiménez', 'NR', 'Los Serrano is a Spanish television drama comedy which premiered on 22 April 2003 and aired on Telecinco. It tells the story of the Serrano family, who lives in Round Santa Justa No 133, located in the fictional neighborhood of Santa Justa, in the Ribera del Manzanares, in Madrid. The success of the series in Spain and in several other countries in Europe and elsewhere helped launch the career of several young actors and actresses, especially actor and musician Fran Perea, who acts in the series and sings its theme song, "1 más 1 son 7".', 'Los Serrano is a Spanish television drama comedy which premiered on 22 April 2003 and aired on Telecinco. It tells the story of the Serrano family, who lives in Round Santa Justa No 133, located in the fictional neighborhood of Santa Justa, in the Ribera del Manzanares, in Madrid. The success of the series in Spain and in several other countries in Europe and elsewhere helped launch the career of several young actors and actresses, especially actor and musician Fran Perea, who acts in the series and sings its theme song, "1 más 1 son 7".', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/w9hPecVLyCkbnJLLdjFu67URBZP.jpg', 8, 'tmdb:tv:7283'),
  ('501982605432690593', 'Los simuladores', 2002, 'Action & Adventure, Comedy', 'Damián Szifron', 'Damián Szifron, Patricio Vega, Diego Peretti', 'Diego Peretti, Sergio Dioguardi, Jorge D''Elía, Federico D''Elía, Alejandro Fiore, Martín Seefeld, César Vianco, Alejandro Awada', null, 'A small team of con artists for hire use their skills to solve common people''s life problems.', 'A small team of con artists for hire use their skills to solve common people''s life problems.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/xGDNHABcl6x1Ulx7Azxg9Dq0ZHL.jpg', 2, 'tmdb:tv:332'),
